     The stock OnePlus camera cannot request runtime permissions on AOSP
     derived systems: its first-run permission flow queries OPLUS framework
     permissions (oplus.permission.*) that do not exist there, aborting
     before the CAMERA dialog is ever shown; the activity then hits
     "onTimeoutWaitingForCameraList" and finishes itself. Pre-grant the two
     permissions required to open the camera pipeline (fixed=false so the
     user can still revoke them in Settings).
-->
<exceptions>
    <exception package="com.oneplus.camera">
        <permission name="android.permission.CAMERA" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO" fixed="false"/>
    </exception>
</exceptions>
